    "narrative": "For this July 6th slate, the Ghost Ride the WHIP offense is anchored by **James Wood** (76.14) and **Corbin Carroll** (72.02). **James Wood** is our premier play, benefiting from a high-upside matchup against Burrows (4.71 xERA) and the prestige of the leadoff spot, which amplifies his elite .425 xwOBA. **Corbin Carroll** remains a priority start despite the moderate xERA of Buehler; his dynamic platoon advantage and projected sprint speed contributions make him an essential engine for our stolen base targets. **Isaac Paredes** also presents a strong profile (68.21), taking full advantage of a favorable park shift and a soft matchup against Mikolas to solidify his position in the heart of our order.\n\nMid-tier decisions were heavily influenced by situational efficiency, with **Kyle Karros** (63.19) emerging as the most significant riser due to a high-leverage matchup against Lauer (5.28 xERA). Conversely, **Dalton Rushing** (41.13) sits right on the fringe of our starting threshold; while his raw talent is clear, the combination of a difficult L/L platoon matchup against Freeland and a low spot in the order suppresses his efficiency score. Among our reserves, **Austin Riley** (59.30) was the last man standing in the lineup; he narrowly edged out the rest of the bench due to his proximity to the 60-point \"Strong\" threshold and a favorable look at the opponent's delivery pace, which theoretically optimizes his chances for a rare steal. We remain vigilant regarding **Trevor Story**, who remains sidelined on the IL, and we are managing our remaining assets like **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Max Muncy**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Alex Freeland**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Edwin Arroyo**, **Cole Young**, and **Henry Bolte** carefully to ensure we stay within our strict game cap constraints while maximizing the impact of every lineup slot.",
